{{Politics of Bolivia}}

A province is the second largest administrative division in [[Bolivia]], after a [[Departments of Bolivia|department]]. Each department is divided into [[province]]s. There are 112 [[province]]s. 

The country's provinces are further divided into 337 [[Municipalities of Bolivia|municipalities]] which are administered by an [[alcalde]] and [[municipal council]].

Unlike departments and municipalities, provinces do not have corresponding government entities or elected officials.<ref>{{Cite| last = Yaksic Feraudy| first = Fabián II| title = AUTONOMÍAS Y ORGANIZACIÓN TERRITORIAL DEL ESTADO| access-date = 2026-05-10| url = http://econstitucional.com/ensayos/Autonom%C3%ADas%20y%20organizaci%C3%B3n%20territorial%20del%20Estado%20F.%20Yaksic.pdf| archive-date = 2013-11-26| archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20131126063414/http://econstitucional.com/ensayos/Autonom%C3%ADas%20y%20organizaci%C3%B3n%20territorial%20del%20Estado%20F.%20Yaksic.pdf| url-status = dead}}</ref>

